  ],
  "notes": "This LER (382-2022-004-00) describes two related but distinct latent calibration-procedure defects: (1) containment high range radiation monitor ARMIRE5400B incorrect conversion factor + keep-alive omission (common cause with ARMIRE5400A from LER 2022-003-00, triggering 50.73(a)(2)(vii)(D) dual-channel reporting), and (2) main steam line radiation monitor ARMIRE5500A missing reference-value recording steps. Both modeled as parallel failure chains under the same official cause code D. ARMIRE5400A itself is referenced as already reported under stub LER 2022-003-00; only its role in the common-cause consequence is modeled here, not a full duplicate failure chain. No BACKED_UP_BY edges emitted for EALs (procedural mitigations, not systems) but alternate dose-assessment methods for ARMIRE5500A are noted as design/operational context in the consequence's mitigation narrative rather than a System node, since no named backup system was stated as operable."
}